	(text "UNTESTED - NOT MANUFACTURED, NOT MEASURED, NOT SAFETY-TESTED. MAINS VOLTAGE (230 V) CAN KILL.\n\nROLAND TR-808 - POWER SUPPLY PS3116-054 (220/240 V), PCB 291-405A\n\nRedrawn from the service manual (15 June 1981): schematic sheet 13, component layout sheet 12,\nparts list sheet 10. Designators and terminal numbers 1-22 as in the original.\n\nBridge rectifiers D1/D2: W04 (400 V, 2W04G on the unit); the manual gives W-02 (200 V);\nthe W04 fits the same package and is a permissible replacement.\n\n220/240 V variant (PS3116-054): C1 ECQ-U2A473MF 0.047 uF, fuses CEE 250 mAT,\ntransformer N-219D, mains switch SDG5P-502. For 100/117 V (PS3116-051): C1 ECQ-UC1A473MC,\nfuses SGA 0.5 A, transformer N-217N/N-218C, switch SDG5P-001; same board.\n\nSecondary voltages at 0.15 A DC: terminals 10-11 (YEL-YEL) 10 V DC, 12-14 (RED-BLK)\n23 V DC (per half). Outputs: +5 V (19), +15 V (22), -15 V (20), 0 V (21),\nRAM supply +5 V / battery 3 x 1.5 V (16, 17).\n\nThe two grounds (5 V branch: 15/18, +-15 V branch: 13/21) are NOT connected on the board in the\noriginal; they meet only outside the board.\nTransformer T1, mains switch and battery are not on the board (terminals 7-14, 4-6, 15/16).\nThe wire jumper J1 of the original (single-sided board) is dropped: this rebuild is two-layer.\nTerminals 1-9 (230 V primary side) are RM5 screw terminals X1-X4; 10-22 are solder lugs.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 340.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "96fd74b8-cd29-4031-8170-4f3e06ebaf4a")
	)
